Core Use Case

I have two Excel workbooks.

Baseline workbook

This represents the previous/current approved version of the Salary Review data.

Working workbook

This is a copy of the Salary Review workbook that users are allowed to modify.

Both workbooks have:

* the same Excel table structure;
* the same table name;
* the same column names;
* the same Employee ID field.

When someone changes monitored Salary Review information in the Working workbook, I want Power Automate to:

1. detect that the Working workbook was modified;
2. determine who modified the workbook;
3. compare the Working workbook with the Baseline workbook;
4. match employees using Employee ID;
5. determine exactly which monitored fields changed;
6. capture the previous and new value;
7. notify a Microsoft Teams channel;
8. create an audit record where configured;
9. update the Baseline after successful processing so the same change is not reported repeatedly.

Example:

Faraz Khan (100236)

Bonus Amount:
£3,000 → £4,000

Changed by: John Smith
Changed: 7 August 2026 14:20

